WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.870
You sketch your idea in R, or in Python.

2
00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:05.720
It is too slow.

3
00:00:05.770 --> 00:00:07.900
So you rewrite it in C.

4
00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:11.070
Julia ends that.

5
00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:13.540
Write it like R. Run it like C.

6
00:00:13.590 --> 00:00:16.540
One language, from sketch to speed.

7
00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:21.020
It began in 2009.

8
00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:26.680
Four people wanted C's speed, R's ease and Python's reach, in one language.

9
00:00:26.730 --> 00:00:29.630
In their words: because we are greedy.

10
00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:33.200
The time of Julia is upon us.

11
00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:36.050
The only question is how to begin.

12
00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:39.150
Julia Time.

13
00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:44.450
Learn Julia by solving a lab mystery with Itchy, Momo, Toto and Eddie.

14
00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:48.250
Six steps, each a lesson and a chapter of the case.

15
00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:52.550
Tables, grouping, joins, then chance and simulation.

16
00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:57.350
Every idea is explained, shown, then yours to try.

17
00:00:57.700 --> 00:01:01.100
Make a mistake, and it tells you what went wrong.

18
00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:05.330
R and Python sit beside every line.

19
00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:11.770
Then put it to work: hit the targets, and see the speed for yourself.

20
00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:38.630
Free, on your own laptop, and nothing is scored.

21
00:01:38.940 --> 00:01:41.190
The time of Julia is now.

22
00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:43.240
Your time starts here.

